# Every text file is checked out with LF line endings, on Windows too
# (Git for Windows' core.autocrlf would otherwise write CRLF). The release
# artifacts, the dashboard's CSP script hash and scripts/*.sh all depend on the
# committed bytes. The Python build backend also packs text as LF, so a CRLF
# checkout can't change a wheel or sdist either.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files: never converted or diffed as text. No binary fixture is
# committed today; these cover the kinds the tests generate or might add.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.whl binary
*.zip binary
*.tar binary
*.gz binary
*.tgz binary
*.pyc binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.node binary
*.wasm binary
*.so binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
